  "product": "GTS",
  "name": "Pure Sine Sub",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "The reference sub: one clean sine at the played pitch with a short soft attack and nothing else, no filter, no distortion, no width. Use it to layer under another bass without adding anything above it, or to check how a system or room handles F1 to A#1. It is mono, and nothing is routed to change the pitch or the tone. Play: long notes in the F1 to A#1 range; below about 40 Hz many speakers give nothing back, so check it on headphones too. Macros: Level trims the output over a 6 dB range (it rests at full), Soft Attack stretches the fade-in from a firm 2 ms to a 40 ms swell, Octave Up blends in a sine one octave above for small speakers, Release stretches the tail from a short 60 ms to about half a second.",
  "category": "Bass/sub",
  "tags": [
    "sub",
    "clean",
    "mono",
    "qa_macro2=Tatt:10",
    "qa_macro4=Trel:50",
    "qa_bright=40..160"
  ],
